'' SWAP, measured from fbc. The most common unlowered intrinsic in the corpus at 841
'' occurrences -- picked by measurement rather than by what looked next in the catalogue.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/swap.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 scope imbalance

'' A STRING pair goes through the runtime, and takes SIX arguments rather than four:
'' each side is (pointer, length, flag) with the flag 0.
'' EXPECT-OUT: call.rtl void fb_StrSwap(@s, -1, 0, @t, -1, 0)

'' Anything else is a temporary and three assignments. THE TEMPORARY IS TYPED TO THE
'' OPERAND: swapping two doubles through an integer slot would round-trip the bits
'' through the wrong register class, so an f64 pair must produce an f64 temp.
'' EXPECT-OUT: local i32 $tmp6
'' EXPECT-OUT: local f64 $tmp7
'' A MIXED-TYPE swap must CONVERT, not reinterpret. fbc emits 'A = fb_D2I( B )' and
'' 'B = (double)TMP', so an fptosi and a sitofp must both appear -- their absence is a
'' silent miscompile that verifies clean.
'' EXPECT-OUT: fptosi
'' EXPECT-OUT: sitofp
'' EXPECT-NOT: <NO TERMINATOR>
'' GOLDEN: expected/swap.out
